  "coverage": {
    "layer_1": "implemented",
    "layer_2": "partial",
    "notes": [
      "SIMPLIFICATION: APPRENTICESHIP PERCENTAGE BASE. Art. G14 §16 states percentages apply to 'minimi tabellari in vigore, indennità di contingenza' (tabellare + contingenza only). EDR per Art. G22 is not subject to the apprenticeship percentage. The engine applies the percentage uniformly to base + seniority + all allowances including EDR. EDR is therefore understated for apprentices. Maximum error per level per month: EDR × (1 − period_pct). Example level 3, period 12–18m (80%): EUR 45.51 × 0.20 = EUR 9.10.",
      "SIMPLIFICATION: APPRENTICESHIP TRACKS. Art. G14 defines 18-month, 24-month, and 36-month tracks with different percentages. Only the 36-month track is modelled (the most common professionalising track).",
      "SIMPLIFICATION: SENIORITY CAP. Art. G23 §5 grants one additional scatto to employees hired before 1 January 1993 reaching 16 years of company seniority from 1 January 2026. The engine has no hire-date input; maximum_count is set to 8 for all workers, understating by 1 scatto for eligible pre-1993 employees.",
      "SIMPLIFICATION: LEVEL 9 SENIORITY. Art. G23 seniority table lists amounts for levels 1S through 8 only. Level 9 is absent. Modelled as 0.00; not confirmed whether intentional exclusion or typographical omission.",
      "SIMPLIFICATION: SUPPLEMENTARY ALLOWANCES. Role-conditional allowances (turno, campo, maneggio denaro, DPI) and the una tantum of EUR 500 (Art. G20, October 2025) are not modelled. All are attendance- or role-conditional or one-time payments.",
      "SIMPLIFICATION: ART. G6 RECLASSIFICATION. A supplementary agreement of 23 March 2026 reportedly amended Art. G6 (professional classification). The amendment text was not retrieved; its effect on level codes and salary tables for as_of dates from 2026-03-01 onward is unverified. Hourly divisor taken from Art. G28 text; no official hourly-rate column available in the source for back-calculation cross-check."
    ]
  },
